opam-version: "2.0"
synopsis: "Virtual package for GCC on i686 mingw-w64, as zcaml's x86_64 toolchain"
description: """\
zcaml's Windows toolchain is x86_64-only and installs `x86_64-w64-mingw32-gcc`.
Upstream's package runs `i686-w64-mingw32-gcc --version`, which that toolchain
doesn't have. This package checks the x86_64 compiler instead: it is what the
64-bit build uses, and nothing here builds 32-bit code."""
maintainer: "David Allsopp <dra27@dra27.uk>"
authors: "The GCC Developers"
license: "GPL-3.0-or-later"
dev-repo: "git+https://github.com/dra27/mingw-w64-shims.git"
homepage: "https://www.mingw-w64.org"
bug-reports: "https://github.com/ocaml/opam-repository/issues"
available: os = "win32"
depends: [
  "conf-mingw-w64-gcc-x86_64"
]
build: [
  ["x86_64-w64-mingw32-gcc" "--version"]
]
